// endpoint_report_composer_draft.proto — ReportComposerDraft: the text a
// workspace's composer held when the editor closed the workspace. FEED
// section.
//
// THE EDITOR CLOSES WHAT IT DOES NOT HOLD (frontend.v1.RosterRowHeld): a
// workspace folded, hidden or left kills its composer in the editor, while the
// daemon keeps the workspace. The composer's text would die with it, so the
// editor reports the text as it closes the workspace, and the daemon keeps it
// durably, across a restart and a handover alike. The next host snapshot after
// the editor opens the workspace again carries it
// (agentrepl.v1.HostWorkspace.composer_draft); the editor puts it into the
// composer, then reports it cleared.
//
// THE REPORT REPLACES the draft the daemon kept, whole. IDEMPOTENT: restating
// the draft the daemon keeps changes nothing.

